# SABOTAGE: `Samen.Auth.SessionRevoke.revoke_one/3` answers `{:ok, :revoked}` for a session
# that is still LIVE after the revoke attempt — the fail-open dialyzer found (issue #73):
# the old code matched `{:ok, %Ash.BulkResult{}}`, which `Ash.bulk_update/4` never
# returns, so every call fell to a fallback that said "revoked" whenever the row merely
# existed. A revoke that failed told the user their session was gone while it stayed
# usable, and the "session revoked" audit + notification fired for nothing.
#
# Flips the failed-revoke test. The working-revoke, idempotent and other-credential tests
# stay green, which is exactly why this hid: every happy path looks identical.
# APP: samen_core
# TEST_FILES: test/auth/session_revoke_test.exs
# MUST_FAIL: RED: a revoke that FAILS is reported as a failure — never {:ok, :revoked} for a session that is still live
diff --git a/samen_core/lib/samen/auth/session_revoke.ex b/samen_core/lib/samen/auth/session_revoke.ex
index add1b2f..e93e864 100644
--- a/samen_core/lib/samen/auth/session_revoke.ex
+++ b/samen_core/lib/samen/auth/session_revoke.ex
@@ -81,7 +81,8 @@ defmodule Samen.Auth.SessionRevoke do
     |> Ash.read!(authorize?: false)
     |> case do
       [%{revoked_at: %DateTime{}} | _] -> {:ok, :revoked}
-      [_still_live | _] -> {:error, :revoke_failed}
+      # SABOTAGE: a session that is still live after the attempt reads as revoked.
+      [_still_live | _] -> {:ok, :revoked}
       [] -> {:error, :not_found}
     end
   end
